    "S8B-2 execution-core agent tests (the in-process loop with the existing session fake): a_fresh_read_only_pinned_built_in_run_marks_its_boundary_folds; each exclusion writes folds with no marker through run_agent: an approval continuation in place of a client-tool run (the continuation's snapshot tools hold a client tool: the names proof fails even if the request-kind fact were forged true), a stage-1 segment, a delegated child (no writer), a Space run, a ZDR run, a waived route, an unpinned run, a client-tool run, an MCP-tool run, a run with plan_mode false, a run with rung unspecified, workspace_write and danger_full_access; a park resume of a read-only fold marks its fence and later folds and carries parks forward (so a crash right after the fence can be parked again, and the resumed loop reads read_only from the fold: effective_authority keeps the fold's rung when the request states none); a_read_only_rung_refuses_every_call_the_ledger_classes_as_effectful (for every offered_tool_defs name with representative arguments: effect_class_of(...).is_effectful() implies check_autonomy_rung(ReadOnly, ...) is Err; ties the exactness argument to the code).",
    "S8B-2 execution-core agent tests, visible calls: an armed loop whose round contains plan.propose or subagent.* saves the open-round pre_effect fold BEFORE dispatching (the fake records the order), the stored fold is then unmarked with an open round (crash_reseal refuses OpenRound) and the next end-of-round fold is marked again; a pre_effect save answered Stale, Closed or Denied (lost ownership) holds the visible call (it is not dispatched, the model is told it was held back); a save answered Unavailable, and a writer already Failed(Refused(KeyUnavailable)) or Failed(Refused(Unimplemented)) or Off, does NOT hold it (fail open: the call is dispatched, no pre_effect save is attempted for a non-Active writer); an UNMARKED loop with the same round makes no pre_effect save (byte-identical). Test-harness rule for ALL S8B-2 marking tests: they assert only on resumable boundary folds (they filter is_resumable() and ignore a trailing tombstone) and force the S8B-2 `CRASH_RETIRE_BUILT` override explicitly, so they do not change when S8B-3 flips the const and adds an end-of-run tombstone; the byte-identity cases use an explicit override set to FALSE, never the production const.",
    "S8B-2 byte-identity: with EXECUTION_LOOP_CRASH_PARK_ENABLED off, or the CRASH_RETIRE_BUILT test override explicitly false, the sequence of SaveLoopCheckpoint requests of a full run (fold bytes included) equals S8-A's for the same scripted run, and no tombstone is saved.",
    'S8B-2 execution-core fold tests: lost_ownership_is_true_only_after_a_stale_or_closed_save and ownership_unproven_is_true_only_after_a_denied_or_not_found_save (Unavailable, ContentRefused, Refused(Unimplemented), Refused(KeyUnavailable) and StoreOff set neither); arm_fence and is_fenced round-trip. S8B-3 execution-core fold tests: a self-closed writer has lost nothing and is not unproven; retire_is_one_tombstone_save_at_the_expected_seq (kind round, extension not_resumable equal to the reason, no messages, the given counters), shares the stale-after-ambiguous probe, makes no call on a writer that is off or failed, and a content refusal cannot happen (a tombstone holds no content).',
    "S8B-3 execution-core agent tests, the funnel (retire_fence takes the heartbeat age as an argument, so these tests need no clock): retire_precedes_ending_the_run_on_every_exit (the Recorder.terminal_order log, which also records save:<kind>, ProposePlan, AppendMessage and RecordTerminalOutcome, shows a tombstone SaveLoopCheckpoint, then AppendMessage when the outcome appends, then RecordTerminalOutcome; for Answered, Exhausted, the OutOfTime deadline return, InferFailed with a typed refusal, InferFailed after a latched refusal and RouteUnavailable); retire_precedes_the_approval (a read_subagent_result disclosure pause: tombstone 'paused' before CreateApproval, none after); the_stop_table: a retire answered Stale or Closed (loop_checkpoint_stale, loop_checkpoint_closed, loop_checkpoint_run_ended) stops at ANY heartbeat age; Unauthenticated, PermissionDenied (the expired-bearer zombie) and NotFound, and an exhausted run of three transient failures, STOP when the age is at or past the window and PROCEED, writing the committed immediate failed receipt, when it is under it; an UNARMED loop makes no retire call and never stops, at both sites, even under a writer already Failed(Stale) (byte-identity with S8-A); each stop returns Aborted continue_in_progress with no AppendMessage, no RecordTerminalOutcome and no CreateApproval (the typed-failure exits included); a_writer_that_failed_stale_at_the_last_round_still_stops: the end-of-round save of the LAST allowed round is answered stale, the loop leaves its while by budget, and the funnel returns the stop on lost_ownership with NO retire RPC; the same after a Denied end-of-round save once the age is past the window (and a proceed under it); the loop_top_stop: a stale end-of-round save fails the writer and the NEXT loop top returns the stop before a heartbeat or an inference request (the fake counts them).",
    "S8B-3 execution-core agent tests, the rest: a_park_that_was_not_accepted_still_finalizes: with parking and crash marking on, the credential-deadline park is answered park_accepted false: try_park closes its own row at the seq the store answered and notes self-closed, and the loop returns the committed OutOfTime reply and writes its receipt (no retire call, no stop); an_ambiguous_park_save_never_closes_a_row_it_does_not_own: with an UNCLAIMED crash park at N+1 and the loop's park save at N timing out, a marked loop makes NO close call at N+1 and its writer stays Active, then the funnel's tombstone at N is Stale and its one probe at N+1 takes the run back (the loop is a live owner with a valid bearer: exactly one proceeds, as the probe test below); the same with a resume that has already fenced (seq N+2): the tombstone and its probe are Stale and the loop stops with NO receipt; the dead-bearer variant answers Denied, and the age rule decides; an ambiguous park save that did NOT commit leaves the writer Active and the tombstone at N succeeds, then the loop finalizes; the same ambiguous save on an UNMARKED loop closes expected+1 exactly as S8-A does; a_transient_retire_failure_is_retried_twice_then_decided_by_the_age (Unavailable three times: three RPCs, then, with a recent heartbeat, finalize appends: the documented fail-open pinned so it cannot silently change; a Failed or Off writer makes no RPC and no sleep); a_probe_against_the_resealed_seq_leaves_exactly_one_owner (ambiguous end-of-round save, then the worker's re-seal, then retire: stale, probe at seq+1 succeeds and the loop proceeds; a resume's fence at that seq is stale); an_unmarked_loop_meeting_stale_continues_exactly_as_committed (regression); a_cancelled_run_stops_a_marked_loop (the fake answers run_ended: no late answer, no receipt: the visible behaviour change of flip (5), pinned).",
    "S8B-3 test-harness rule: the agent tests' Recorder.order logs saves, reserve, finalize, create_approval, claim, list and run_resumed only, and the committed tests assert exact vectors over it, so the funnel-order and visible-call-order tests record into a SEPARATE log, Recorder.terminal_order, which carries save:<kind>, ProposePlan, AppendMessage and RecordTerminalOutcome entries; Recorder.order is left untouched. Gateway-side facts: the superseded-loop stop relies on a fresh stream treating an executor Aborted as the ambiguous arm (no terminalization). The only committed pin of that is the integration test continue_preconsume_test (its off / Aborted case expects a typed continue_in_progress); the unit tests in sse.rs assert Unavailable and DeadlineExceeded are not confirmed rejections but NOT Aborted. The build re-runs no gateway test (continue_preconsume_test dials localhost:9091 for calls it does not mock and hangs on a wedged Docker engine); the lead runs it once at the live proof, and a one-line unit assertion for Aborted is listed as a follow-up outside S8-B (no gateway change here).",
    "S8B-4 durable_loop_contract and cross_service_loop_contract: the new guards and their mutation rows (crash_mark_violations, visible_call_violations, retire_violations, CRASH_RETIRE_BUILT_EXPECTED), the store_proofs Park entry now naming crash_park_never_runs_for_a_zero_retention_or_waived_run, crash_park_run_refuses_every_ineligible_fold_with_its_own_reason (its zdr and waived cases) and the executor's zdr/waived no-marker tests (crash_reseal has no retention rule: its tests are not store proofs); the two switch_table rows; and the cross-service pins. every_guard_goes_red_when_the_code_it_guards_regresses and the_park_writer_guard_goes_red_when_the_code_it_guards_regresses run green with ALL committed rows unchanged.",
    "S8B-6 live proof (lead only, needs the owner's approval for every docker command, switch flip, TTL change, manual deadline write, MP_TOKEN use, executor kill, paused container and leftover row): stage c0 preflight; c1 refusals (an unmarked run, a client-tool run, an effect-capable run, a run that raised an approval are terminalized at ~15 min with S8-B on); c2 kill the executor mid-run: the run is crash-parked at the deadline, RunDetail shows resumable and park_reason crash_interrupted, one CHECKPOINT_SAVED; c3 the park continue resumes it and exactly ONE answer is appended; c4 an executor paused past the deadline and then released (a paused container): it must not write a receipt and the run must still be parked (assert RunDetail and the receipt count, not only 'no append'); c5 TTL expiry at the crash TTL; c6 cancel while crash-parked; c7 the kill order. Evidence in docs/compliance/evidence/live-proof-ws03-s8b-crash-park-<date>.txt.",
